WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.070
Harry: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:03.330
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:05.660
between Oreos in the UK and the US.

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:07.670
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:09.390
Hey, everyone. Joe from "Food Wars."

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:12.730
I will not be partaking
in this episode of Oreos

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:14.820
because me and the team are busy shooting

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.450
a new season of "Food
Wars" with a new country.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.830
That's right, coming soon to you

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:22.660
it's going to be "Food
Wars" US versus [beep].

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:24.513
While we're working hard
on that, Irene, of course,

00:00:24.513 --> 00:00:26.100
is going to step in
over there in New York.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.970
I will, however, stick
around for this episode

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:31.543
and make smart-alecky comments
because that's my brand.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:35.380
In the UK, Oreos come
in four serving sizes.

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:37.079
As a lunch-box pack of two,

00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:38.680
as a standard pack of 14,

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:40.530
as a twin pack of 28,

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:43.060
and as an open and share pack of 36.

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:46.328
In the US, classic Oreos
come in six serving sizes.

00:00:46.328 --> 00:00:48.561
As a two-cookie snack pack,

00:00:48.561 --> 00:00:50.411
as a six-cookie snack pack,

00:00:50.411 --> 00:00:53.100
as a king-size 10-cookie snack pack,

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.828
as a classic pack of 36 cookies,

00:00:55.828 --> 00:00:58.230
as a family-size pack of 48 cookies,

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:02.281
and, finally, as a party-size
pack of 63 cookies.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:06.110
The cookies themselves
are supposed to weigh

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:08.350
the same amount in both
countries, 11 grams.

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:10.024
We're going to weigh one
and find out if that's true.

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:13.690
12.4 grams.

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:15.137
We're going to do the scientific method.

00:01:15.137 --> 00:01:17.700
We're going to test a second cookie

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:19.663
in case there's any disparities.

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:23.017
Yeah, 11.4.

00:01:23.017 --> 00:01:25.400
You know what, I bet it's the frosting.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:28.720
This one's 11.8 grams.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.370
Yeah, this one's 11.5.

00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:33.550
So the average weight is 11.8 grams.

00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:36.110
So, our UK Oreo weighed 11.09 grams.

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:37.760
Pretty much spot on what they promised us.

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:39.400
The portion sizes aren't the only thing

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.100
that's different between our Oreos.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:44.210
The US also has more Oreo size options.

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:46.010
There are the mini Oreos,

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:48.251
then five stuff options:

00:01:48.251 --> 00:01:49.592
Oreo thins,

00:01:49.592 --> 00:01:50.950
classic Oreo,

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:52.092
Double Stuf,

00:01:52.092 --> 00:01:53.025
Mega Stuf,

00:01:53.025 --> 00:01:56.000
and then The Most Stuf.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:57.770
I didn't know The Most Stuf existed.

00:01:57.770 --> 00:01:59.990
I thought we ended it at Double Stuf.

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:01.290
We kept going.

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:02.256
I have an idea.

00:02:02.256 --> 00:02:03.472
I don't know why they haven't done this,

00:02:03.472 --> 00:02:05.123
'cause the Stuf is what everybody wants,

00:02:05.123 --> 00:02:06.073
at least in America.

00:02:06.073 --> 00:02:08.350
Oreo needs to invent Just Stuf.

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:12.580
It is a sandwich cookie: Stuf, Stuf, Stuf.

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:13.944
Check it out!

00:02:13.944 --> 00:02:16.373
Just Stuf Oreos.

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:20.350
Perfect. That's all I want.

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:24.990
Whereas our options are
minis, thins, classic,

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:26.392
or Double Creme.

00:02:26.392 --> 00:02:28.044
For some some reason we call
them Double Creme over here

00:02:28.044 --> 00:02:28.882
and not Double Stuf.

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:32.760
How much Stuf are we actually getting?

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:35.077
Let's dissect a classic Oreo.

00:02:40.543 --> 00:02:42.510
2.52 grams.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.590
We're committing to 3.2 grams.

00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:46.425
Is a Double Stuf Oreo actually giving you

00:02:46.425 --> 00:02:47.258
double the Stuf?

00:02:47.258 --> 00:02:48.416
Let's find out.

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:51.473
Oh, look at that precision.

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:54.490
Earlier was 3.2.

00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:56.015
So this is 6.

00:02:56.015 --> 00:02:58.168
That came to 6.13 for us.

00:02:58.168 --> 00:03:00.644
They got a little bit
more. That never happens!

00:03:00.644 --> 00:03:01.609
[gasps]

00:03:01.609 --> 00:03:03.030
So, in the UK, Double Creme Oreos

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:06.510
actually give you 143% more
filling than the classic Oreo.

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:10.742
While a US Double Stuf has 87.5% more Stuf

00:03:10.742 --> 00:03:12.280
than a classic Oreo.

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:14.597
I want to know how much
the Most Stuf weighs.

00:03:15.696 --> 00:03:17.180
Oh, wow.

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:18.350
This is excessive.

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:22.060
So, the Most Stuf weighs 11.2 grams,

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:25.640
which is a 250% increase from the classic.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:26.946
It's very stabbable.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:30.920
I'm gonna DIY my own giant Oreo.

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:33.240
I don't know if it's gonna
fit in my mouth, but.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:36.180
Harry Makes the World's
Largest Oreo -- ASMR.

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:37.230
11.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:43.930
It is about 3 inches. Ish.

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:45.810
It's falling apart, much like me.

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:46.950
You know what has to happen now.

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:47.783
I mean, come on.

00:03:47.783 --> 00:03:48.720
"Had to happen"?

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:49.707
"Had to happen," Harry?

00:03:49.707 --> 00:03:51.537
This had to happen?

00:03:51.537 --> 00:03:53.986
I'm gonna squeeze it down.

00:03:53.986 --> 00:03:55.315
There we go.

00:03:55.315 --> 00:03:56.148
Yo!

00:04:05.327 --> 00:04:07.810
[crew clapping]

00:04:09.178 --> 00:04:10.942
God, you need the biscuit, really.

00:04:12.817 --> 00:04:15.010
Yeah, as you can see, maybe,

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:17.002
maybe all that stuffing at
once is not a good idea.

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:20.280
Here are all of the UK Oreo products

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:21.880
that you won't find in the US.

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:24.410
Here are all the Oreo products in the US

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:26.490
you won't find in the UK.

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:28.400
Oreo lends its brand name
to a lot of products.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:29.660
So we're going to split
this into sections,

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:31.000
starting with the cookies.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.080
That's nothing compared to us.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:37.450
We have 20 exclusive Oreo
cookie flavors in the US.

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:39.280
We have two exclusive
classic Oreos in the UK,

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:42.173
starting with these ones, which
are strawberry cheesecake.

00:04:42.173 --> 00:04:43.898
Can't figure out --

00:04:43.898 --> 00:04:45.006
ooh.

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:50.676
It's very good.

00:04:50.676 --> 00:04:51.509
Then we have this one,

00:04:51.509 --> 00:04:53.470
which is a chocolate
brownie batter flavor.

00:04:56.840 --> 00:04:58.430
The flavor of the chocolate filling

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:01.170
kind of gets lost in just
the chocolate cookie flavor.

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:04.110
Peanut butter flavor cream. Creme?

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:06.670
I do think some people put
peanut butter on their Oreos,

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:08.140
so maybe that's where this came from.

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:10.270
The Mega Stuf.

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:13.959
'Cause Double Stuf was
simply not enough for us.

00:05:13.959 --> 00:05:16.520
Like, honestly, though,
I can appreciate this,

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:18.980
'cause I always want more of the frosting.

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:21.965
But this is kind of ridiculous, isn't it?

00:05:21.965 --> 00:05:24.800
We have gluten-free Oreos.

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:28.940
Lemon flavor creme Oreos.

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:32.515
This seems like a golden
Oreo with lemon filling.

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:37.720
It has the Oreo structure,

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:39.910
but it's like a whole completely
different flavor profile,

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:41.151
so it tastes really good.

00:05:41.151 --> 00:05:42.522
[beeps]

00:05:42.522 --> 00:05:43.839
[screams]

00:05:43.839 --> 00:05:45.988
Oreos are too popular in this country.

00:05:45.988 --> 00:05:47.229
We don't need this many flavors.

00:05:47.229 --> 00:05:48.062
[beeps]

00:05:48.062 --> 00:05:48.895
As we move through this section,

00:05:48.895 --> 00:05:50.170
you're going to notice a
bit of a Cadbury theme,

00:05:50.170 --> 00:05:52.170
because Cadbury and Oreo
seem to have partnered up

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:53.250
on quite a few products.

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:55.490
The first one we have here
is a Cadbury-coated Oreo.

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:57.080
Now, these are just basic Oreos,

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:58.970
but then covered in Cadbury chocolate,

00:05:58.970 --> 00:05:59.803
which, as we all know,

00:05:59.803 --> 00:06:01.395
is much better than American chocolate.

00:06:04.010 --> 00:06:06.080
They're so good, but so bad for you.

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:07.420
Then, after that, we
have these little bags

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:08.840
of Oreo crunchy bites.

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:12.040
These come as either classic
or as dipped versions.

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:12.960
I'm not really sure how they differ

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:14.730
from just classic mini Oreos,

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:16.451
so I'm gonna open a bag and find out.

00:06:17.501 --> 00:06:18.990
Is that not just a mini Oreo

00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:20.517
that they've rebranded?

00:06:20.517 --> 00:06:22.810
In my left hand, I'm holding
an Oreo crunchy bite.

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:25.110
In my right hand, I'm holding a mini Oreo.

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:26.520
The only notable difference is maybe

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:29.130
that the mini Oreo has
slightly more filling.

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:31.113
I feel like this is just
an excuse to sell you

00:06:31.113 --> 00:06:33.598
maybe even less stuffed mini Oreos

00:06:33.598 --> 00:06:34.930
at a more expensive price point.

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:36.350
Companies can't get away with this anymore

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:37.670
now that "Food Wars" exists.

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:40.145
Chocolate hazelnut.

00:06:40.145 --> 00:06:43.050
This is basically like if
you put Nutella in an Oreo.

00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:44.533
Caramel coconut.

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:47.883
I think you would like
this if you like caramel.

00:06:47.883 --> 00:06:49.220
Chocolate marshmallow.

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:52.200
Ooh, I think this one does
have something on the biscuit.

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:53.260
That's different.

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:54.591
Oh, it's on the inside.

00:06:54.591 --> 00:06:55.440
I thought it would be on the outside.

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:56.490
That'd be more fun, but.

00:06:58.530 --> 00:06:59.640
Yeah, you get the chocolate flavor,

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:01.234
but I don't think the
marshmallows really come through.

00:07:01.234 --> 00:07:02.067
[beeps]

00:07:02.067 --> 00:07:03.384
Is anyone even eating these?

00:07:03.384 --> 00:07:04.970
I have never seen a single person

00:07:04.970 --> 00:07:06.880
buy any of these flavored ones.

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:08.220
So this feels like a conspiracy.

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:09.053
[beeps]

00:07:09.053 --> 00:07:11.040
We have the java chip.

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:13.431
Supposedly there'll be
little chocolate chips.

00:07:15.699 --> 00:07:16.720
This is good. This reminds me of, like,

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:19.630
a Starbucks java chip
Frappucino, honestly.

00:07:19.630 --> 00:07:20.920
Dark chocolate.

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:24.570
The original was just simply
not chocolaty enough for you.

00:07:24.570 --> 00:07:26.310
It matches the biscuit.

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:28.324
OK, I'm actually really
excited about this one.

00:07:28.324 --> 00:07:30.840
They're Olympic Oreos!

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:32.260
Aah!

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:33.640
I'm one of those people who is like,

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:34.819
I could have been an Olympian

00:07:34.819 --> 00:07:36.880
if my parents had just loved
me enough to, you know,

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:39.613
make it my entire life
and forced me to do it.

00:07:39.613 --> 00:07:42.150
You know, as if that's all it takes.

00:07:42.150 --> 00:07:45.350
"Red, white, and blue layers
of cream with popping candy."

00:07:45.350 --> 00:07:47.630
Oh, these layers are so uneven.

00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:49.120
It's funny.

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:50.875
You see this? It's like ...

00:07:50.875 --> 00:07:53.391
A while ago, they had
special Fourth of July ones

00:07:53.391 --> 00:07:55.097
that had, like, sparklers or something,

00:07:55.097 --> 00:07:57.360
and it was basically the same
thing, the popping candy.

00:07:57.360 --> 00:07:59.200
I feel like they're kind
of just reusing this.

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:00.560
Oh, wait, this is cool too.

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:03.530
It has the Olympic circles
and the American flag.

00:08:03.530 --> 00:08:04.920
You know, the best part
about the Olympics this year

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:06.874
has just been all the Olympians on TikTok,

00:08:06.874 --> 00:08:09.600
and then also how funny it
is that everyone's like,

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:13.945
"We're only patriotic about
how funny and hot they are."

00:08:13.945 --> 00:08:15.230
If any Olympians are watching this,

00:08:15.230 --> 00:08:16.760
I am in fact single. Thank you.

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:20.765
When did "Food Wars"
become Irene's dating app?

00:08:20.765 --> 00:08:22.080
She didn't say which Olympians, though.

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:24.362
So, like, the Canadian curling
team's coming after her.

00:08:24.362 --> 00:08:25.207
So watch out.

00:08:27.390 --> 00:08:28.920
The next one, which is
still kind of a cookie,

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:31.197
are these Cadbury
Crunchy Melts Oreo Creme.

00:08:31.197 --> 00:08:32.030
Now, these are kind of big,

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:33.430
more traditional chocolate chip cookies,

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:35.660
but then filled with
a layer of Oreo creme.

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:38.110
I will say the packaging
made me expect a lot more

00:08:38.110 --> 00:08:39.610
of the Oreo creme in the middle there.

00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:40.969
It's a very, very thin layer.

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:45.447
I'm really disappointed by that.

00:08:45.447 --> 00:08:46.940
I was -- I had high hopes for these.

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:49.158
The texture of the cookie is way off.

00:08:49.158 --> 00:08:52.870
Ooh, salted caramel brownie Oreos.

00:08:52.870 --> 00:08:54.840
They're really just turning
every possible dessert

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:56.420
into an Oreo at this point.

00:08:56.420 --> 00:08:58.020
But, again, I have never
seen a single person

00:08:58.020 --> 00:08:59.150
buy one of these.

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:01.500
If you are someone who buys
these, please let me know.

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:04.619
'Cause I think it's a
conspiracy at this point.

00:09:04.619 --> 00:09:06.330
Ooh, this one also is a double layer.

00:09:06.330 --> 00:09:08.410
We have a light brown layer
and a dark brown layer.

00:09:08.410 --> 00:09:11.000
Ooh, and then there's salt on the biscuit.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:12.620
They really elevated this one.

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:14.136
It's like a gourmet Oreo.

00:09:16.386 --> 00:09:18.370
I actually really like
the salt on the biscuit.

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:20.260
It comes together really nicely.

00:09:20.260 --> 00:09:22.143
Again, this is weird.

00:09:22.143 --> 00:09:24.309
Carrot cake. Who thought of this?

00:09:24.309 --> 00:09:26.017
Carrot cake's hard to get right.

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:30.910
Tastes like ginger with
just, like, nice icing.

00:09:30.910 --> 00:09:32.580
So I actually like these,

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:33.610
but that's 'cause they don't taste

00:09:33.610 --> 00:09:35.546
like the advertised flavor.

00:09:35.546 --> 00:09:36.379
[beeps]

00:09:36.379 --> 00:09:38.750
I'm doing really bad, Shirley.

00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:40.800
I'm trying not to cry, I think?

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:42.042
I'll be alive.

00:09:42.042 --> 00:09:43.540
I don't think the Oreos will kill me.

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:45.751
Actually, the Oreos might kill me!

00:09:45.751 --> 00:09:47.840
I can't believe this is
what's gonna take me out.

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:49.179
It's gonna be the Oreos.

00:09:49.179 --> 00:09:50.012
[beeps]

00:09:50.012 --> 00:09:52.003
Chocolate peanut butter pie.

00:09:52.003 --> 00:09:55.070
How many variations of chocolate
peanut butter do we need?

00:09:55.070 --> 00:09:56.530
I will say, they are creative, right?

00:09:56.530 --> 00:09:58.730
It's not like they just,
like, blast it with flavors

00:09:58.730 --> 00:09:59.590
and it looks the same.

00:09:59.590 --> 00:10:01.418
At least they look fun.

00:10:04.487 --> 00:10:05.320
[beeps]

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:07.870
I thought the Oreos would
make me feel better.

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:09.530
They made me feel worse.

00:10:09.530 --> 00:10:11.203
I was betrayed by the Oreos.

00:10:12.393 --> 00:10:13.226
[beeps]

00:10:13.226 --> 00:10:16.240
Limited-edition s'mores.

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:18.820
Graham-flavored cookies.

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:22.630
These are the golden Double Stuf Oreos.

00:10:22.630 --> 00:10:27.077
It's literally the non-chocolate
version of a regular Oreo.

00:10:27.077 --> 00:10:28.060
Aah.

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:29.663
I have an announcement to make.

00:10:29.663 --> 00:10:32.787
Golden Oreos are the best Oreo.

00:10:32.787 --> 00:10:34.540
That's right, the best.

00:10:34.540 --> 00:10:35.490
These are the best.

00:10:35.490 --> 00:10:36.323
Look at me.

00:10:36.323 --> 00:10:38.389
Look at me, YouTube commenters.

00:10:38.389 --> 00:10:40.955
This is the best Oreo there is.

00:10:40.955 --> 00:10:43.570
I have access to the Food
Insider YouTube page,

00:10:43.570 --> 00:10:45.630
and I will delete your comments
if you disagree with me.

00:10:45.630 --> 00:10:47.778
This is the best Oreo.

00:10:49.962 --> 00:10:50.795
Amazing.

00:10:50.795 --> 00:10:53.140
So, there's also three
fudge-covered flavors,

00:10:53.140 --> 00:10:56.680
classic, dark chocolate, and mint.

00:10:56.680 --> 00:10:58.620
There's also these Oreo thin bites

00:10:58.620 --> 00:11:00.911
in original and white fudge.

00:11:00.911 --> 00:11:04.870
So these are basically mini
Oreos covered in chocolate.

00:11:04.870 --> 00:11:07.336
And, of course, the Oreo ID,

00:11:07.336 --> 00:11:09.511
which are customizable Oreos.

00:11:09.511 --> 00:11:11.780
We decided to decorate
it with white sprinkles

00:11:11.780 --> 00:11:15.625
and put Joe's face on it since
we missed him this episode.

00:11:15.625 --> 00:11:17.149
I guess you could call them

00:11:17.149 --> 00:11:18.841
J'oreos.
[drum sting]

00:11:18.841 --> 00:11:20.010
That's such a good idea!

00:11:20.010 --> 00:11:20.843
Why don't we have that?

00:11:20.843 --> 00:11:23.885
That's such a funny, like,
party gift, wedding favor.

00:11:23.885 --> 00:11:24.890
Just a lot of potential there,

00:11:24.890 --> 00:11:26.080
and I kind of wish we had that.

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:27.005
Look, it's Joe!

00:11:27.005 --> 00:11:28.520
"Ha, ha, ha, ha.

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:31.978
I'm in LA, and I eat food and do things,

00:11:31.978 --> 00:11:33.247
and I have a podcast."

00:11:33.247 --> 00:11:34.305
I don't have a podcast.

00:11:34.305 --> 00:11:36.959
I am the last human being on
the planet to have a podcast.

00:11:36.959 --> 00:11:38.657
Comment below what my podcast should be

00:11:38.657 --> 00:11:39.523
and who I should have on it.

00:11:39.523 --> 00:11:41.748
Sorry, Joe. I'm gonna
cut your face in half.

00:11:46.176 --> 00:11:47.878
I didn't think I would be
saying this of all people.

00:11:47.878 --> 00:11:49.620
It's just a lot of sugar.

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:50.870
It's too much sugar.

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:52.340
Yeah, I don't want these.

00:11:52.340 --> 00:11:53.813
Joe, you can have them.

00:11:55.670 --> 00:11:57.495
All right, let's take a look at these.

00:12:02.780 --> 00:12:04.289
Yeah, these don't taste like Oreos.

00:12:04.289 --> 00:12:05.130
These aren't very good.

00:12:05.130 --> 00:12:06.750
Sorry. I taste terrible, apparently.

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:09.320
Then we have a section
I'm really excited for,

00:12:09.320 --> 00:12:11.140
which is the frozen dessert section.

00:12:11.140 --> 00:12:12.823
We'll start with these,
which are Oreo ice creams

00:12:12.823 --> 00:12:14.750
with an Oreo cookie coating.

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:15.883
Ooh.

00:12:15.883 --> 00:12:16.716
Hm.

00:12:19.890 --> 00:12:21.620
It's not the best ice cream I've ever had.

00:12:21.620 --> 00:12:23.670
Very sweet and a bit, like, foamy.

00:12:26.090 --> 00:12:27.410
OK, the cone's pretty good.

00:12:27.410 --> 00:12:30.080
I'd say this would maybe get
better the more you go down.

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:31.660
I think less of the ice cream on the top,

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:32.540
and more of the cone.

00:12:32.540 --> 00:12:33.900
The next ice cream option is this one,

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:36.370
which is the Oreo ice cream
with Oreo biscuit pieces.

00:12:36.370 --> 00:12:37.710
In the UK, we can also just get a tub

00:12:37.710 --> 00:12:39.000
of Oreo-branded ice cream.

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:40.162
Now, ones which I've had before

00:12:40.162 --> 00:12:42.320
and can tell from experience are very good

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:44.579
are these ones, which are the
Oreo ice cream sandwiches.

00:12:48.815 --> 00:12:49.729
Mm.

00:12:49.729 --> 00:12:51.010
Then we're back to the Cadbury partnership

00:12:51.010 --> 00:12:53.250
with these Cadbury-coated
stick sandwiches.

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:55.589
Our Oreo desserts in the US include

00:12:55.589 --> 00:12:57.903
Breyers Oreo Chips Ahoy ice cream

00:12:57.903 --> 00:13:00.542
and Friendly's Oreo
cookies ice cream cake.

00:13:00.542 --> 00:13:01.683
What!

00:13:01.683 --> 00:13:03.600
See, this is a good dessert combo.

00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:04.433
This makes sense.

00:13:04.433 --> 00:13:07.650
You're adding the Oreos
to an existing thing.

00:13:07.650 --> 00:13:08.913
Wow.

00:13:10.860 --> 00:13:13.885
Ugh, ice cream cakes are
always so hard to cut.

00:13:15.727 --> 00:13:17.300
Cake!

00:13:17.300 --> 00:13:18.133
[crowd gasps]

00:13:19.303 --> 00:13:20.136
Ta-da.

00:13:20.136 --> 00:13:21.580
And we weren't able to get these,

00:13:21.580 --> 00:13:25.010
but there's also Klondike
Oreo ice cream sandwiches,

00:13:25.010 --> 00:13:26.850
Good Humor Oreo ice cream bars,

00:13:26.850 --> 00:13:29.190
and Good Humor Oreo cones.

00:13:29.190 --> 00:13:30.850
Then we have a bunch of
exclusive chocolate options,

00:13:30.850 --> 00:13:32.370
which are, again, mostly Cadbury.

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:34.990
This one is a dairy milk Oreo sandwich.

00:13:34.990 --> 00:13:37.160
This one is also available
in the form of Cadbury bites,

00:13:37.160 --> 00:13:39.360
which is just bite-sized
pieces of their chocolate bars.

00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:40.402
Then we're on to the one in the middle,

00:13:40.402 --> 00:13:43.260
which is the Cadbury Big
Taste Oreo crunch bar.

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:44.280
If milk chocolate isn't your thing,

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:47.161
then they also have a Cadbury
Oreo white chocolate bar.

00:13:47.161 --> 00:13:48.500
Our final chocolate bar is this one,

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:51.562
which is an Oreo Milka
Mmmax chocolate bar.

00:13:51.562 --> 00:13:53.170
Milka is just a slightly
different chocolate brand

00:13:53.170 --> 00:13:54.190
here in the UK.

00:13:54.190 --> 00:13:55.830
Then we have a couple of
options for baked goods,

00:13:55.830 --> 00:13:58.501
including this Oreo muffin
and this Oreo doughnut.

00:13:59.751 --> 00:14:01.638
I mean, if that counts as a filling,

00:14:01.638 --> 00:14:03.505
again, a little bit underwhelming.

00:14:06.150 --> 00:14:07.990
I know I ate that from the
bottom, like a psychopath.

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:08.993
I don't do that all the time.

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:13.110
This end bit looks slightly filled.

00:14:13.110 --> 00:14:13.943
They put it on the box.

00:14:13.943 --> 00:14:15.952
It's supposed to look like this.

00:14:15.952 --> 00:14:17.519
That's what you call false advertising.

00:14:20.120 --> 00:14:21.220
If you're going to go for one of these,

00:14:21.220 --> 00:14:22.460
probably go for the muffin.

00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:23.910
Then we have a couple more
miscellaneous products

00:14:23.910 --> 00:14:24.800
just to round out.

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:27.720
Here are our miscellaneous Oreo items.

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:30.740
We have the ready-to-bake pie crust.

00:14:30.740 --> 00:14:33.820
And then the instant
pudding pie filling mix,

00:14:33.820 --> 00:14:35.560
which is cookies and cream flavored.

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:37.280
So these go together.

00:14:37.280 --> 00:14:39.790
This is the no-bake Oreo dessert kit,

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:43.420
which is basically these
two items in a box.

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:44.253
The first one is this,

00:14:44.253 --> 00:14:46.410
which is a Cadbury Oreo
hot chocolate powder.

00:14:46.410 --> 00:14:47.360
Now, I'm fascinated by this one

00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:48.830
because when I was
buying it on the website,

00:14:48.830 --> 00:14:51.780
it had loads of one-star reviews
saying it tasted horrible,

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:53.269
so obviously we now have to try it.

00:14:53.269 --> 00:14:56.286
I'm going to use my colleague
Charlie's wonderful mug,

00:14:56.286 --> 00:14:57.710
which I think he got in a charity shop,

00:14:57.710 --> 00:14:59.547
which is celebrating
the marriage of a couple

00:14:59.547 --> 00:15:01.005
who we don't know.

00:15:01.005 --> 00:15:02.620
Buchi and Wumi, if you're watching this,

00:15:02.620 --> 00:15:03.590
I hope you've had a happy marriage.

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:05.390
Four heaped teaspoons of the powder

00:15:05.390 --> 00:15:06.390
into your boiling water,

00:15:06.390 --> 00:15:07.870
which is what I have in here,

00:15:07.870 --> 00:15:09.353
and we should end up with a delicious

00:15:09.353 --> 00:15:10.753
Oreo-flavored hot chocolate.

00:15:10.753 --> 00:15:11.586
So let's go.

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:16.030
Now I'm just gonna stir
for about 40 minutes

00:15:16.030 --> 00:15:17.885
and then see what we end up with.

00:15:17.885 --> 00:15:18.880
[beeps]

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:20.405
Protect me, Buchi and Wumi.

00:15:23.083 --> 00:15:24.108
[coughs]

00:15:24.108 --> 00:15:25.349
Wow, OK. Um.

00:15:25.349 --> 00:15:27.048
The immediate taste you get is chocolate,

00:15:27.048 --> 00:15:27.956
which you expect,

00:15:27.956 --> 00:15:30.080
but then, like, a second after every sip,

00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:32.300
something just kind of
punches you in the face,

00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:33.470
and it's not very pleasant.

00:15:33.470 --> 00:15:34.760
Moving swiftly on from the hot chocolate,

00:15:34.760 --> 00:15:38.010
we have this, which is
an Oreo split-pot yogurt.

00:15:38.010 --> 00:15:39.690
Yes, it's pronounced
"yaugh-gurt" and not "yo-gurt."

00:15:39.690 --> 00:15:40.523
Get it right.

00:15:40.523 --> 00:15:41.390
Do Americans have Müller corners?

00:15:41.390 --> 00:15:43.140
Because I ate those all the
time growing up in the UK,

00:15:43.140 --> 00:15:44.940
and this is the exact
style they've gone for.

00:15:44.940 --> 00:15:46.500
Basically, it's like a split-pot thing

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:47.750
where half of it is yogurt,

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:50.240
and then a little corner of
it is a topping of some kind,

00:15:50.240 --> 00:15:53.851
the idea then being
that you just crack this

00:15:53.851 --> 00:15:55.160
and deposit all the toppings in.

00:15:55.160 --> 00:15:56.290
This really does take me back.

00:15:56.290 --> 00:15:57.860
I would have some kind of Müller corner

00:15:57.860 --> 00:15:59.350
in most of my pack lunches

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:00.434
when I was in primary school.

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:04.273
That's really tasty.

00:16:04.273 --> 00:16:05.670
And then last but by no means least

00:16:05.670 --> 00:16:07.910
we have these, which are Oreo O's.

00:16:07.910 --> 00:16:09.830
Now, it's an Oreo-themed breakfast cereal,

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:11.589
and it comes with these chocolaty loops

00:16:11.589 --> 00:16:13.500
and then some vanilla-flavored disks.

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:15.660
We have the Oreo cereal,

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:17.464
and these look like the UK version,

00:16:17.464 --> 00:16:19.050
but without the white puffs.

00:16:19.050 --> 00:16:23.215
And then we also have Funfetti
brownie mix, cake mix,

00:16:23.215 --> 00:16:26.060
and frosting with Oreo pieces.

00:16:26.060 --> 00:16:28.912
And, lastly, these are
the Oreos Handi-Snacks,

00:16:28.912 --> 00:16:31.170
Oreo cookie sticks and cream.

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:32.670
Oh, my God, no.

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:33.728
These look like --

00:16:33.728 --> 00:16:35.770
you know those cheese and cracker snacks?

00:16:35.770 --> 00:16:38.061
This looks like the Oreo version.

00:16:38.061 --> 00:16:39.036
Oh, my God.

00:16:39.036 --> 00:16:40.252
Oh, it looks disgusting.

00:16:40.252 --> 00:16:43.100
There's, like, a pool of oil
or something right there.

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:46.360
Here are all the ingredients
in a classic Oreo

00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:48.101
in the UK.

00:16:48.101 --> 00:16:50.040
That makes a total of
at least 18 ingredients,

00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:52.080
possibly more if multiple
flavorings are used.

00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:56.450
Here are all the ingredients
in a classic Oreo in the US.

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:59.327
That comes to a total of
at least 17 ingredients,

00:16:59.327 --> 00:17:01.400
again dependent on the flavorings used.

00:17:01.400 --> 00:17:02.963
So a UK Oreo actually contains

00:17:02.963 --> 00:17:04.513
more ingredients than a US Oreo.

00:17:04.513 --> 00:17:07.670
The UK has a few ingredients
not found in the US.

00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:09.070
Take sunflower lecithin,

00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:11.320
which they use in
addition to soy lecithin.

00:17:11.320 --> 00:17:13.670
Some people prefer to
use sunflower lecithin,

00:17:13.670 --> 00:17:16.410
as it's extracted naturally
via cold pressing,

00:17:16.410 --> 00:17:19.510
whereas soy lecithin tends to
be extracted using chemicals

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:23.340
such as acetone, like
in nail-polish remover.

00:17:23.340 --> 00:17:24.610
Soybeans are also more commonly

00:17:24.610 --> 00:17:26.402
genetically modified than sunflowers,

00:17:26.402 --> 00:17:28.215
and concerns over this
have also driven people

00:17:28.215 --> 00:17:29.925
away from soy and towards sunflower

00:17:29.925 --> 00:17:31.370
as their preferred source of lecithin.

00:17:31.370 --> 00:17:34.540
In the US, we use high-fructose
corn syrup in our Oreos,

00:17:34.540 --> 00:17:37.370
compared to the UK's
glucose and fructose syrup.

00:17:37.370 --> 00:17:39.320
You'll see this in a lot
of American products,

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:41.770
as it's a cheaper
alternative to actual sugar

00:17:41.770 --> 00:17:45.060
as a result of the US
producing a huge amount of corn

00:17:45.060 --> 00:17:46.810
and tariffs on imported sugar.

00:17:46.810 --> 00:17:48.210
There's limited evidence that suggests

00:17:48.210 --> 00:17:49.740
that high-fructose corn
syrup is worse for you

00:17:49.740 --> 00:17:50.573
than normal sugar.

00:17:50.573 --> 00:17:51.867
Nations which use it tend to have

00:17:51.867 --> 00:17:53.414
higher rates of Type 2 diabetes

00:17:53.414 --> 00:17:54.410
than those that don't.

00:17:54.410 --> 00:17:57.700
What about Oreos with some
more controversial ingredients?

00:17:57.700 --> 00:17:59.660
Like birthday cake, for example.

00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:02.020
In the UK, we actually call
those birthday party Oreos,

00:18:02.020 --> 00:18:03.430
but they are effectively the same thing.

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:06.310
In the UK, we color the
sprinkles with spirulina extract,

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:08.470
red beet juice, and turmeric extract.

00:18:08.470 --> 00:18:10.990
Whereas in the US, we
color our sprinkles with

00:18:10.990 --> 00:18:14.760
Yellow 5, Blue 1, Red 40, and Red 3.

00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:17.770
Fans of "Food Wars" will
recognize Yellow 5 and Red 40

00:18:17.770 --> 00:18:20.770
as two food colorings
not often seen in the UK.

00:18:20.770 --> 00:18:22.530
If they are used in the UK,

00:18:22.530 --> 00:18:24.250
manufacturers have to add a warning

00:18:24.250 --> 00:18:27.390
that they, "May have an
adverse effect on activity

00:18:27.390 --> 00:18:29.010
and attention in children."

00:18:29.010 --> 00:18:32.420
We love our artificial
and potentially dangerous

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:33.910
food colorings over here.

00:18:33.910 --> 00:18:34.970
Red 3 is actually one

00:18:34.970 --> 00:18:36.550
I don't think we've seen
before on "Food Wars."

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:37.916
It's otherwise known as erythrosine,

00:18:37.916 --> 00:18:40.410
and it's a dye used to give
foods a reddish-pink color.

00:18:40.410 --> 00:18:42.300
It's not commonly used in the US,

00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:45.240
with manufacturers usually
opting for Red 40 instead.

00:18:45.240 --> 00:18:47.076
The reason for its low popularity

00:18:47.076 --> 00:18:49.610
is its association with
certain health effects.

00:18:49.610 --> 00:18:52.260
It was partially banned in the US in 1990

00:18:52.260 --> 00:18:55.778
after research showed that
it caused cancer in rats.

00:18:55.778 --> 00:18:57.654
Its use is restricted
in the European Union

00:18:57.654 --> 00:18:58.910
due to the same concerns.

00:18:58.910 --> 00:19:00.410
While the European Food Safety Authority

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:02.193
did say that humans weren't
at quite the same risk

00:19:02.193 --> 00:19:03.481
of tumors that rats were,

00:19:03.481 --> 00:19:06.308
they still set a limit of 0.01 milligrams

00:19:06.308 --> 00:19:09.360
per kilogram of body weight
per day for human consumption.

00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:11.778
As a result, the only food
that Red 3 can be used in

00:19:11.778 --> 00:19:13.720
in the EU is candied cherries.

00:19:13.720 --> 00:19:16.690
It's not banned in the
US, but it is restricted.

00:19:16.690 --> 00:19:17.960
It can be added to foods,

00:19:17.960 --> 00:19:21.370
but it can't be put in
cosmetics or external drugs.

00:19:21.370 --> 00:19:25.692
So you can put it in your
body, but not on your body.

00:19:25.692 --> 00:19:27.000
Other things to look out for in the US

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:29.610
include the carrot cake Oreos,
which contain caramel color.

00:19:29.610 --> 00:19:30.880
According to the state of California,

00:19:30.880 --> 00:19:33.089
a byproduct of this can cause cancer,

00:19:33.089 --> 00:19:35.253
birth defects, or other reproductive harm.

00:19:37.364 --> 00:19:39.600
The UK's Oreo is actually
healthier in every metric

00:19:39.600 --> 00:19:42.000
other than saturated fat,
where the two are tied.

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:44.098
Classic Oreos aren't too unhealthy,

00:19:44.098 --> 00:19:46.294
except for the sugar content.

00:19:46.294 --> 00:19:48.940
You would only have to eat 11 US Oreos

00:19:48.940 --> 00:19:51.090
to hit your entire daily sugar allowance,

00:19:51.090 --> 00:19:54.460
which is just under a third
of your daily calories.

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:56.330
What about the least healthy
Oreo in each country?

00:19:56.330 --> 00:19:58.500
Well, in the UK, it's
the Cadbury-coated Oreo.

00:19:58.500 --> 00:20:00.790
Here's the nutritional
information for just one of them.

00:20:00.790 --> 00:20:01.860
If you eat just five of these,

00:20:01.860 --> 00:20:03.920
you consume 98% of your daily sugar

00:20:03.920 --> 00:20:06.170
and 55% of your daily saturated fat.

00:20:06.170 --> 00:20:07.610
And I'm pretty sure if
I started eating these,

00:20:07.610 --> 00:20:09.170
I would be eating more than five.

00:20:09.170 --> 00:20:10.924
Our least healthy Oreo?

00:20:10.924 --> 00:20:13.730
It's the fudge-covered
dark chocolate Oreo.

00:20:13.730 --> 00:20:15.280
Five of these cookies would be

00:20:15.280 --> 00:20:18.496
110% of your daily sugar allowance

00:20:18.496 --> 00:20:22.888
as well as 112.5% of
your daily saturated fat.

00:20:22.888 --> 00:20:24.820
I don't know if I want to eat these.

00:20:24.820 --> 00:20:26.040
These are aggressive.

00:20:26.040 --> 00:20:29.650
I feel like Joe could probably
eat, like, the entire box.

00:20:29.650 --> 00:20:30.875
I'll try one.

00:20:30.875 --> 00:20:32.332
It says "mmm."

00:20:32.332 --> 00:20:33.807
I don't feel "mmm."

00:20:33.807 --> 00:20:36.835
We don't need to cover
everything with chocolate.

00:20:36.835 --> 00:20:38.410
[sighs]

00:20:38.410 --> 00:20:40.375
Something about this seems wrong.

00:20:44.253 --> 00:20:46.170
It actually is good. Very chocolaty.

00:20:46.170 --> 00:20:50.220
It tastes -- oh, my God, the
filling is chocolate too!

00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:51.400
Joe can have these.

00:20:51.400 --> 00:20:52.580
Joe, you can eat these.

00:20:52.580 --> 00:20:53.540
Irene, I don't want those.

00:20:53.540 --> 00:20:54.450
Don't send them over here.

00:20:54.450 --> 00:20:56.040
Off to LA!

00:20:56.040 --> 00:20:57.840
Ah, there.

00:20:57.840 --> 00:20:59.760
No, thanks.

00:20:59.760 --> 00:21:01.170
Well, the monster,

00:21:01.170 --> 00:21:03.306
the monster one was 11 Double Stufs,

00:21:03.306 --> 00:21:04.172
so that's, like, 20,

00:21:04.172 --> 00:21:06.788
that's literally 22 cookies, Shirley.

00:21:06.788 --> 00:21:09.060
And then I had at least three or four,

00:21:09.060 --> 00:21:10.883
and I took several bites of others,

00:21:10.883 --> 00:21:13.553
so I have had at least 30 to 40 cookies

00:21:13.553 --> 00:21:15.752
if you do the math, honestly.

00:21:15.752 --> 00:21:18.118
And then you add that
I didn't eat breakfast,

00:21:18.118 --> 00:21:19.720
and then you add that I'm in the midst

00:21:19.720 --> 00:21:21.490
of, like, five mental breakdowns,

00:21:21.490 --> 00:21:23.490
and so we are in an interesting place.

00:21:23.490 --> 00:21:27.592
Just gonna roll away.

00:21:27.592 --> 00:21:30.244
[laughing]

